# A branch mutation changes an adaptive element's integer base

Verifies a conditional write that promotes an `int64` element to `int128`
keeps the later dynamic read and chained operation on the promoted base.

>>> source
let values: int[] = [1]
if (true) {
    values[0] = 9223372036854775807 + 1
}
print(values[0] + 1)

<<< stdout
9223372036854775809

<<< stderr
